<title-page
title: The Ethnography of the Silly Computer
author: Tyler Childs

Premise

We all use technology every day but we will never meet the people, or elves, that lived full, rich, real lives and died building the things in our hands. Wait. What if we literally could meet them? Would that create a paradox?

Witness that paradox.

SHOW TIMES

5 pm
2.5 hours bar room, cocktail reception
7:30pm curtain
10 minute monologue
15 minute monologue
10 minute monologue
10 minute monologue
10 minute musical performance
20 page minutes/bumper sketches
5 minute panel interview
5 minute panel interview
5 minute panel interview
5 minute musical performance
10 minute jam capture
9:15 pm curtain, Video Stream Cut
Yellow Balloon Jam Session until Last Call, Audio Stream Cut

