# Stand-up

The first clown nose, "You ever have one of those really bad days?" "What is it going to take to break me for me to become an emergency clown?"

The flute, the barrel, and the balls. Who I am and where I'm from. Massachusetts not even being named correctly due to misinformation. Massasoit means Great Sachem and the colonists just thought that was his name because everyone called him that. Massachusetts should be derived from his true name, which has been lost to time despite him warning the pilgrims of an attack against them in time.

JD Vance is just Trey Falwell in drag, we were all on 18-2. We knew we were the gay hall, right boys? Van, Vaniel, VanBob.

My time travel adventure into north beach. Ruby. Toby. Lost Church.

Greatest gamer of all time. The Onion. World of World of Warcraft. Halo, Steve Jobs, Microsoft, 1984, Apple Jonathan

riff on an alternate reality where the mac lost internally to the jonathan and microsoft ceased to exist once DOS was just pages in a book, and the macbook was just a book on the jonathan, the same way sillyz computer is "just" a flying disk.

! hang out in this space with the audience until i get the light or i lose them--

Giants, Crazy Crab, Mascots, Red Sox, World Series, Paul Revere's ghost, Fired from Netflix.

What happened to me at Netflix?

They said, "You are bad at using computers to elevate the quality of our productions. Go now. Busk."

I muttered under my breath, "did the algorithm pay you to say that?" and they didn't ask "What" because they didn't care. Everyone on their way out says something or other in the end, but my final words were "Silly Synthia." as the door slammed shut behind me. But I didn't say Silly.

 # Scene 1 - NINTENDO

Clay as Ty and Ty as Nintendo

@ NINTENDO
> Remember when we hired you?

@ Tyler
> Yeah. Those were good days.

@ NINTENDO
> Still are, right?

@ Tyler
> I mean, they're pretty good.

@ NINTENDO
> Pretty good? Do you know how many men, women, and children want to be inside me?

@ Tyler
> I love my job. I just feel, there used to be more passion in why we even bother to make art at all.

@ NINTENDO
> Look at our numbers, they're the best!

@ Tyler
> The best is still yet to come, but we are in a slump right now. These numbers are artificial. Everyone was too afraid to leave the house for a couple years.

@ NINTENDO
> Oh no. You're right. Look. A bad trend.

@ Tyler
> Yeah, exactly, that's what I'm saying. We have to compete with  the outdoors again. This is the attention economy, right?

@ NINTENDO
> Oh no. Oh no no no. The trend is growing. Growing bad. Down growing. Double plus ungood.

@ Tyler
> That's the outdoors. Reality is calling the people. We're a mere reflection of the truth they seek.

@ NINTENDO
> Don't use big words to try to confuse me.

@ Tyler
> I'm sorry.

@ NINTENDO
> You know what? You should be. You are bad at using computers to elevate the quality of our games. Go now. Busk.

@ Tyler
> Did the algorithm tell you to say that?

Tyler begins walking off stage, the door closing behind him

@ Tyler
> What am I doing, I live here. Get the silly out of my house, Synthia!

NINTENDO runs out, the door slamming shut behind.

